                <pb facs="0732" n="630" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg630"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 2151/74.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Spanish Chargé to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Spain</hi><lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-10-21"><hi rendition="#italic">October 21,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary</hi>: I have the honor to inform your
                    excellency that I am advised by cablegram from my Government that the copy of
                    the circular relative to the indemnities on account of the Casablanca incident
                    intended for the Federal Government was mailed from Madrid on the 16th
                    instant.</p>
                <p>I shall lose no time in handing the document to your excellency as soon as it
                    reaches me, and in the meantime I beg to say that it is substantially the same
                    as the circular of the Paris cabinet on the same subject, a summary of which I
                    understand was delivered to Mr. Bacon day before yesterday by the French
                    ambassador.</p>
                <p>I avail, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">L. Pastor.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
